From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: ingenic: tcu: keep a PWM the bootloader left running

Every timer channel was reset (control register cleared, clock stopped)
when its clock was registered, very early in boot. A backlight PWM the
bootloader left on (h2boot shows its boot logo) went dark there and stayed
dark until the display driver enabled the backlight, most of a second
later. Leave a channel that is running with its PWM output enabled as it is.
---
--- a/drivers/clk/ingenic/tcu.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/ingenic/tcu.c
@@ -282,10 +282,25 @@
 	tcu_clk->info = info;
 	tcu_clk->tcu = tcu;
 
-	/* Reset channel and clock divider, set default parent */
-	ingenic_tcu_enable_regs(&tcu_clk->hw);
+	/*
+	 * Reset channel and clock divider, set default parent. Except for a
+	 * channel the bootloader left running as a PWM (a backlight showing its
+	 * boot logo): reset, the light would go out until its driver starts it
+	 * again. Its parent and divider are then read back as they are.
+	 */
+	if (ingenic_tcu_enable_regs(&tcu_clk->hw) && idx < tcu->soc_info->num_channels) {
+		unsigned int ter = 0, tcsr = 0;
+
+		regmap_read(tcu->map, TCU_REG_TER, &ter);
+		regmap_read(tcu->map, info->tcsr_reg, &tcsr);
+		if ((ter & BIT(idx)) && (tcsr & TCU_TCSR_PWM_EN)) {
+			pr_info("ingenic-tcu: timer %u left running by the bootloader as a PWM: kept\n", idx);
+			goto keep;
+		}
+	}
 	regmap_update_bits(tcu->map, info->tcsr_reg, 0xffff, BIT(parent));
 	ingenic_tcu_disable_regs(&tcu_clk->hw);
+keep:
 
 	err = clk_hw_register(NULL, &tcu_clk->hw);
 	if (err) {
